          "solution": "```python\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef fisher_optimal_binary_cat_split(categories, y) -> tuple[list[str], float]:\n    cats = np.asarray(categories)\n    ya = np.asarray(y, dtype=float)\n    n = float(len(ya))\n    p_par = float(ya.mean())\n    g_par = 2.0 * p_par * (1.0 - p_par)\n    stats = []\n    for c in np.unique(cats):\n        m = (cats == c)\n        cnt, pos = float(np.sum(m)), float(np.sum(ya[m]))\n        stats.append((pos / cnt, str(c), cnt, pos))\n    stats.sort(key=lambda item: (item[0], item[1]))\n    best_gain, best_left = -1.0, []\n    tot_pos, cum_n, cum_pos = float(ya.sum()), 0.0, 0.0\n    for k in range(len(stats) - 1):\n        cum_n += stats[k][2]\n        cum_pos += stats[k][3]\n        rem_n, rem_pos = n - cum_n, tot_pos - cum_pos\n        pL, pR = cum_pos / cum_n, rem_pos / rem_n\n        gain = g_par - (cum_n / n) * (2.0 * pL * (1.0 - pL)) - (rem_n / n) * (2.0 * pR * (1.0 - pR))\n        if gain > best_gain:\n            best_gain = gain\n            best_left = sorted(item[1] for item in stats[: k + 1])\n    return (best_left, round(float(best_gain), 4))\n```"
