          "starterCode": "import numpy as np\n\ndef audit_monotonicity_violations(predict_fn, X_base, feat_idx: int, direction: int, grid_values, tol: float = 1e-9) -> tuple[int, int, float]:\n    X_arr = np.asarray(X_base, dtype=float)\n    grid = np.sort(np.asarray(grid_values, dtype=float))\n    # TODO: evaluasi predict_fn sepanjang grid pada kolom feat_idx, hitung diffs = direction * np.diff(preds, axis=1)\n    pass\n\ndef buggy_credit_scorer(X: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n    dti = X[:, 0]\n    score = 0.2 + 0.7 * dti - 0.25 * np.exp(-((dti - 0.80) / 0.06) ** 2) + 0.05 * X[:, 1]\n    return np.clip(score, 0.0, 1.0)\n\nX_b = [[0.3, 0.0], [0.5, 1.0], [0.4, 2.0]]\ngrid_dti = [0.20, 0.40, 0.65, 0.80, 0.90]\nprint(audit_monotonicity_violations(buggy_credit_scorer, X_b, feat_idx=0, direction=1, grid_values=grid_dti))",
