          "solution": "```python\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef audit_monotonicity_violations(predict_fn, X_base, feat_idx: int, direction: int, grid_values, tol: float = 1e-9) -> tuple[int, int, float]:\n    X_arr = np.asarray(X_base, dtype=float)\n    grid = np.sort(np.asarray(grid_values, dtype=float))\n    preds = np.zeros((len(X_arr), len(grid)), dtype=float)\n    for k, gv in enumerate(grid):\n        Xm = X_arr.copy()\n        Xm[:, feat_idx] = gv\n        preds[:, k] = np.asarray(predict_fn(Xm), dtype=float)\n    diffs = float(direction) * np.diff(preds, axis=1)\n    viol_mask = diffs < -tol\n    n_viol_rows = int(np.sum(np.any(viol_mask, axis=1)))\n    n_viol_steps = int(np.sum(viol_mask))\n    max_viol = float(max(0.0, -float(np.min(diffs))))\n    return (n_viol_rows, n_viol_steps, round(max_viol, 4))\n```"
